**WAKE.** Today's personas found no new physics. The algebra they rechecked by hand all held. Two items do reach the research record, and both are correct verdicts pinned to the wrong thing, so I wrote a proposal before fixing the site:
- **"MOND's V⁻² excluded at ~10σ"** (on three pages and in the PREDICTIONS ρ_crit row). That 10σ is about the framework's own Jeans-construction knee, not MOND. MOND's transition density falls as V⁻² by construction on any sample obeying the BTFR, and this regression doesn't test it. As written, the sentence read as a 10σ result against MOND.
